{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/287037-sin-eater-as-a-support-character","id":287037,"title":"Sin-Eater as a support character?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-19T17:58:13-07:00","id":287037,"title":"Sin-Eater as a support character?","content":"So, in my current group, we are in a game that is fairly combat intensive at times and my current character is no longer playable due to hitting Morality zero due to some unfortunate circumstances. We have since gained another player who is a front line fighter and I thought I may as well take up a support character instead.<br /> <br /> My question is are Sin-Eaters capable of fulfilling this role? Or am I better off picking up a different game Archetype instead? If so, suggestions on either how to build the Sin-Eater or which other Archetype I should pick are greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T21:14:05-07:00","id":287234,"title":"","content":"You can make a support Sin-Eater. It is not the path of least resistance, but powers like Boneyard, Curse, Marianette, Oracle and Pit are mostly not combat oriented, and some other Manifestations have non combat uses. I guess depends on what you mean by &quot;support&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T04:17:37-07:00","id":287443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/287037-sin-eater-as-a-support-character?p=287234#post287234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess depends on what you mean by &quot;support&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question, especially since I realize that unlike a Mage, as a Sin-Eater you can't fulfill traditional support roles such as being a healer. I was hoping to be a support in a way similar to a being a giant nuisance for enemies. Enemies don't hit my allies as hard, they hit the wrong people, some get lost along the way and wind up in the wrong room, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 10-20-2014, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T04:53:27-07:00","id":287453,"title":"","content":"Depends on the scenario. Sin-Eaters can be great informants and has a wide variety of ways to solve a number of diverse issues and disable enemies with curses and phantasms. However, in a combat scenario, a Sin-Eater does best when he is killing things or preventing things from killing him. He cant place his Shroud on his teammates like a Mage might and the Curses he can place are more annoying as long-term issues than immidiate threats. While he is able to heal his allies, he doesn't do it quite as effectively as a Mage might, nor is his phantoms as effective at way-laying people in the short-term.<br /> Honestly, if you're gunning for a support role in terms of a combat scenario, a Mage would be the way to go. Preferably something the lines of Mind/Space/Prime/Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T09:17:05-07:00","id":287718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/287037-sin-eater-as-a-support-character?p=287453#post287453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, if you're gunning for a support role in terms of a combat scenario, a Mage would be the way to go. Preferably something the lines of Mind/Space/Prime/Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was sort of hoping that wouldn't be the case since I am not a huge fan of Mage in particular. I feel they overshadow the other archetypes by being pretty much best at everything. That, and I like the whole concept of Sin-Eaters more. <br /> <br /> What is curious to me though is you say that Sin-Eaters do best when killing things, but I thought doing that is an automatic drop of Synergy?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T11:27:01-07:00","id":287873,"title":"","content":"Outright murder of someone helpless is an automatic Synergy drop. Sin-Eaters do not lose Synergy from killing almost any other time, unless it is completely accidental or purposeless. So they are among the few who can kill all they want without losing Morality unless the subject is quite helpless or they have no reason.<br /> <br /> Mages do make better &quot;Support&quot; characters, but that does not limit you to them. The question is what are you looking for as &quot;support&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-20-2014, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T14:46:08-07:00","id":287986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/287037-sin-eater-as-a-support-character?p=287873#post287873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outright murder of someone helpless is an automatic Synergy drop. Sin-Eaters do not lose Synergy from killing almost any other time, unless it is completely accidental or purposeless. So they are among the few who can kill all they want without losing Morality unless the subject is quite helpless or they have no reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is where I am confused still, on page 173 under Last Resort it says the following, <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 173</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">New death is murder: cold-blooded, intentional murder. The act of murder creates a temporary link between a Sin-Eater and his victim, through which he can harvest the energy of death. Deaths caused in self-defense or that happen as accidents don't create the necessary bond. Only the raw, dark emotion born of violence and sin that accompanies murder allows a Sin-Eater to profit from the death of another. A Sin-Eater that intentionally murders someone is fully healed, but he automatically loses a point of Synergy as a consequence of giving himself over fully to death.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages do make better &quot;Support&quot; characters, but that does not limit you to them. The question is what are you looking for as &quot;support&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to say an untraditional support. On the non-combat side of things, help find things, solve puzzles, help people get into places, make people forget things. On the combat side, hinder enemies either by causing them to not show up on time, make them weaker, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T15:36:49-07:00","id":288028,"title":"","content":"One could interpert that as &quot;no killing&quot; completely, but it is a fairly conservative interpretation, and makes Reapers wholly nonviable as concepts. I won't say what is best for people's game, but the intention is to draw a difference between combat and killing helpless or near helpless victims. But I am not your GM.<br /> <br /> Powers like Curse, Pit, and Boneyard are excellent for Support. In the campaign I am running an APing here, I'd call two of the characters (Natalie and Simon) support characters by that definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T15:40:27-07:00","id":288030,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eaters have several options for those kind of support roles, and can do a few of them very powerfully, but they kind of become a lot more specialized than other templates do. Starting characters only get 3 dots of manifestations (which are pretty expensive to purchase up), and the super-useful abilities tend to be unlocked at 2-4 dots. Three dots in Oracle [particularly with the Stigmata, Industrial, Phantasmal, or an Elemental Key] can get tons of information and bonuses to Social rolls or using objects, etc - but that's about the only trick a starting character will have.<br /> <br /> Boneyard, I think, has a lot of the power's you're looking for in a support-style role. With enough dots and the right keys you can turn your allies invisible, harass enemies with illusions, learn all of the details of a location, toss objects around... It has the limits of only being a static radius around you, and you remain comatose (thus vulnerable) while boneyard is active, but it offers a wide range of &quot;haunting effects&quot; across a large area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T16:05:49-07:00","id":288039,"title":"","content":"Ahh I see, thanks a lot Baron for that interpretation. I will try and clear it with my GM before I try something like this just to be sure. As for why I wanted Sin-Eater over Mage, I am not a huge fan of the environment that Mage creates. When you can do practically anything, choices mean much less. I value the theme and experience far more than power gaming the system which is easy.<br /> <br /> Seraph, thanks for those suggestions, I will look into those and find out how much bonus EXP my GM will be providing me. From there I will see the powers that unlock and see which Manifestation would be worthwhile. Will look at Boneyard first since that does seem like what I would like to do. Stay safe, setup an area of influence ahead of time, and unleash chaos. As there are other non-combat characters, they would probably serve as a good lookout for my character while he is in comatose mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T16:46:04-07:00","id":288062,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, the problem with that rule is it is tight and vague at the same time. It's in one place and not in Synergy (which makes more sense for it) and goes somewhat against how Sin-Eaters are discussed (Angel of Death being a viable concept in theory). Conservatively, killing anyone who does not attack you first or you kill accidentally (a Synergy check, by the way) fully heals you and automatically removes synergy. Liberally, it has to be murder, so you essentially don't apply it to people if you can justify it somehow. The middle road seems to be if you use it to kill some helpless person it counts, but &quot;I am the winning combatant&quot; does not apply. It IS something you want to discuss with your GM, but I would say any deliberate killing at all makes it very difficult and would be something discussed in the book. After all, say Diablorie which is generally an automatic loss is discussed repeatedly as a major sin and has that backing it up. But Sin-Eaters as angels of death is treated casually, and that is not even referenced outside that section. Ectophagia is mentioned in worse terms, and it is a mid-chart roll. One HR (and it is an HR, not interpretation) I saw several times when it came out was if you deliberately kill someone and decide to take the heal, it is a Synergy loss while if you kill someone and don't, it is not a loss. I am mid-road to liberal, so never implemented it as it never seemed necessary. That said, given my druthers, I might make that HR the way it worked in a hypothetical 2e depending on how Synergy-as-Integrity worked.<br /> <br /> In addition to that rule, discuss Plasm with your GM. Plasm can be hard to come by if you are not regularly resolving ghosts. In 1.0, haunts give 1-5 per week, in 1.1 per night, it is good to know which way your GM is going there. Also consider your Threshold's way of getting it back. But Plasm is harder to come by than, say, Glamour or Vitae.<br /> <br /> Boneyard, Curse, and Pit are excellent for Support in terms of surveillance and impairing foes. Oracle is very useful for info gathering. Marianette is useful for dealing with ghosts, making zombies, manipulating people, or similar. But don't forget your Ceremonies! Sin-Eaters get real flexibility from those and some are very useful! Also very ghost focused, but you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T17:02:08-07:00","id":288070,"title":"","content":"Interestingly enough, my GM is running a chronicle based upon Voice of the Angel and we have probably dealt with more ghosts that I care to think about. My party, without the presence of a Sin-Eater has actually been to the Underworld twice. This current time (2nd time), and one of the reasons why a Sin-Eater popped into my head, is the party, in an effort to find out more about the Angel of Death, is traveling to find someone named Mictlan in the depths of the Underworld. If all goes well, I am also hoping my character can meet up with the rest of the party while they travel and hence be a fairly plausible way for me to be introduced.<br /> <br /> Hell, the safehaven where our players gather was once haunted by a ghost who tried to get us to leave. It was an ultra pain to get rid of being that none of us at the time had any real way of interacting with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T00:19:01-07:00","id":288408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/287037-sin-eater-as-a-support-character?p=288062#post288062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, the problem with that rule is it is tight and vague at the same time. It's in one place and not in Synergy (which makes more sense for it) and goes somewhat against how Sin-Eaters are discussed (Angel of Death being a viable concept in theory). Conservatively, killing anyone who does not attack you first or you kill accidentally (a Synergy check, by the way) fully heals you and automatically removes synergy. Liberally, it has to be murder, so you essentially don't apply it to people if you can justify it somehow. The middle road seems to be if you use it to kill some helpless person it counts, but &quot;I am the winning combatant&quot; does not apply. It IS something you want to discuss with your GM, but I would say any deliberate killing at all makes it very difficult and would be something discussed in the book. After all, say Diablorie which is generally an automatic loss is discussed repeatedly as a major sin and has that backing it up. But Sin-Eaters as angels of death is treated casually, and that is not even referenced outside that section. Ectophagia is mentioned in worse terms, and it is a mid-chart roll. One HR (and it is an HR, not interpretation) I saw several times when it came out was if you deliberately kill someone and decide to take the heal, it is a Synergy loss while if you kill someone and don't, it is not a loss. I am mid-road to liberal, so never implemented it as it never seemed necessary. That said, given my druthers, I might make that HR the way it worked in a hypothetical 2e depending on how Synergy-as-Integrity worked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally make the interpritation, that what the Sin-Eater does is he siphons the life-force out of a dying person, ala that one Mage spell, but just much more proficiently. It has to be a concious choice though, you cant drink somebodys life-force by accident. It makes sense that devouring another persons essence for the express purpose of sustaining yourself, would cause Synergy loss, especially since it skews the balance of life and death.<br /> I am not a fan of the auto-loss, though. I just usually make people roll like 1 die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T00:32:57-07:00","id":288410,"title":"","content":"Dess: Well it certainly sounds like you could be useful. If you are looking at Boneyard or Marianette, consider Stigmata, but before taking it you may want to give your GM a heads up; it is very strong against ghosts.<br /> <br /> Krobeles: That makes perfect sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T09:56:12-07:00","id":288643,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice everyone. I believe I am going to create a Sin-Eater with the Industrial and Phantasmal keys who focuses on Boneyard and Curse for the moment. Boneyard for active manipulation and Curse for those targets we interact with, and a more subtle approach is needed. Depending on the amount of experience I would begin with, I may also take a few dots in Shroud for the ability to deceive people in person. Overall, it looks to be exactly the kind of character I was looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}